  "slug": "anvesh-2026-focus-on-sustainable-healthy-foods",
  "summary": "The National Institute of Food Technology Entrepreneurship and Management, Kundli (NIFTEM-K), will organise ANVESH–2026, an international conference dedicated to promoting sustainable and healthy food systems.",
  "content": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>The National Institute of Food Technology Entrepreneurship and Management, Kundli (NIFTEM-K), an Institute of National Importance under the Ministry of Food Processing Industries (MoFPI), will organise ANVESH–2026. The international conference will focus on advancing sustainable and healthy food systems in alignment with global nutrition and sustainability goals.</p><p>The event aims to bring together researchers, policymakers, entrepreneurs, and industry leaders to deliberate on innovations in food technology and sustainable nutrition.</p><h2>About NIFTEM-K</h2><p>NIFTEM-K operates under the Ministry of Food Processing Industries and plays a key role in promoting research, innovation, and entrepreneurship in food technology.</p><ul><li>Recognised as an Institute of National Importance</li><li>Focuses on food processing research</li><li>Supports startup incubation</li><li>Encourages industry-academia collaboration</li></ul><p>The institute contributes to strengthening India’s food processing ecosystem.</p><h2>Theme of ANVESH–2026</h2><p>The conference will emphasize sustainable food production, nutritional security, and technological innovation.</p><ul><li>Climate-resilient agriculture</li><li>Functional and fortified foods</li><li>Food waste reduction technologies</li><li>Alternative protein sources</li><li>Food safety and quality assurance</li></ul><p>The focus aligns with global discussions on food sustainability and public health.</p><h2>Importance of Sustainable Food Systems</h2><p>Sustainable food systems are essential for balancing environmental protection, economic viability, and social equity.</p><ul><li>Reducing greenhouse gas emissions</li><li>Ensuring nutritional security</li><li>Promoting circular economy models</li><li>Enhancing supply chain resilience</li></ul><p>Such systems contribute to achieving Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly SDG 2 (Zero Hunger) and SDG 12 (Responsible Consumption and Production).</p><h2>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</h2><p>ANVESH–2026 will provide a platform for startups and innovators in the food processing sector.</p><ul><li>Technology transfer opportunities</li><li>Research commercialization</li><li>Public-private partnerships</li><li>Investment networking</li></ul><p>Encouraging entrepreneurship is central to expanding India’s food processing industry.</p><h2>Policy Relevance</h2><p>The conference aligns with national initiatives such as:</p><ul><li>PM Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme</li><li>Atmanirbhar Bharat initiatives</li><li>National Nutrition Mission (Poshan Abhiyaan)</li></ul><p>Policy integration ensures practical outcomes from academic discussions.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>ANVESH–2026 represents a strategic effort to integrate sustainability, nutrition, and innovation in India’s food sector. By promoting research collaboration and entrepreneurial growth, the conference aims to strengthen food security and foster environmentally responsible production systems.</p><h2>Exam Perspective</h2><ul><li>Institution: NIFTEM-K</li><li>Ministry: Ministry of Food Processing Industries</li><li>Theme: Sustainable Food Systems</li><li>Relevant for UPSC GS-III (Agriculture & Food Processing)</li></ul><h2>Sources</h2><p>NIFTEM-K Official Announcement 2026, MoFPI Reports</p>",
