  "title": "MoEFCC Hosts Him-CONNECT at WSDS 2026",
  "slug": "moefcc-hosts-him-connect-at-wsds-2026",
  "summary": "The Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change (MoEFCC) is organising ‘Him-CONNECT’ during the World Sustainable Development Summit (WSDS) 2026 to strengthen sustainable development strategies for Himalayan states.",
  "content": "<h2>Introduction</h2><p>The Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change (MoEFCC) is organising ‘Him-CONNECT’ as part of the World Sustainable Development Summit (WSDS) 2026. The initiative focuses on sustainable development, ecological resilience, and climate adaptation strategies for India’s Himalayan region.</p><p>The event highlights the importance of coordinated action among Himalayan states to address climate vulnerability and environmental challenges.</p><h2>About WSDS</h2><p>The World Sustainable Development Summit (WSDS) is an annual global event organised by The Energy and Resources Institute (TERI).</p><ul><li>Platform for global sustainability dialogue</li><li>Participation from policymakers, scientists, and industry leaders</li><li>Focus on climate change and green development</li><li>Promotes Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)</li></ul><p>WSDS serves as a forum for shaping environmental governance and climate policy discourse.</p><h2>Objective of Him-CONNECT</h2><p>Him-CONNECT aims to bring together stakeholders from Himalayan states to discuss region-specific environmental issues.</p><ul><li>Climate adaptation strategies</li><li>Disaster risk reduction</li><li>Biodiversity conservation</li><li>Sustainable tourism models</li><li>Water resource management</li></ul><p>The initiative seeks collaborative frameworks for sustainable Himalayan development.</p><h2>Importance of the Himalayan Region</h2><p>The Himalayan ecosystem is ecologically fragile and strategically significant.</p><ul><li>Source of major rivers</li><li>High biodiversity hotspot</li><li>Climate-sensitive zone</li><li>Prone to landslides and glacial melt</li></ul><p>Climate change impacts such as glacier retreat and extreme weather events pose serious challenges.</p><h2>Policy Relevance</h2><p>The programme aligns with national and international commitments, including:</p><ul><li>National Action Plan on Climate Change (NAPCC)</li><li>Paris Agreement commitments</li><li>SDG 13 (Climate Action)</li><li>Green growth and sustainable development initiatives</li></ul><p>Regional coordination enhances policy effectiveness and implementation.</p><h2>Environmental Governance Focus</h2><p>Him-CONNECT emphasizes multi-level governance involving:</p><ul><li>Central ministries</li><li>State governments</li><li>Scientific institutions</li><li>Local communities</li></ul><p>Community participation and indigenous knowledge integration are key components.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>MoEFCC’s organisation of Him-CONNECT at WSDS 2026 reflects India’s commitment to safeguarding the Himalayan ecosystem through collaborative and science-based approaches. Strengthening ecological resilience in the region is essential for sustainable development, disaster preparedness, and long-term climate adaptation.</p><h2>Exam Perspective</h2><ul><li>Ministry: MoEFCC</li><li>Event: World Sustainable Development Summit (WSDS)</li><li>Theme: Climate Change & Himalayan Sustainability</li><li>Relevant for UPSC GS-III (Environment & Climate Change)</li></ul><h2>Sources</h2><p>MoEFCC Press Release 2026, WSDS Official Documentation</p>",
